description: Sigil workspace boundary across compiler, runtime, registry, ToolForge, and CLI crates
includes:
  - crates/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/Cargo.toml
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/Cargo.toml
  - crates/sigil-runtime/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/Cargo.toml
  - crates/sigil-registry/.scope
  - crates/sigil-registry/Cargo.toml
  - crates/sigil-cli/.scope
  - crates/sigil-cli/Cargo.toml
  - .editorconfig
  - .gitattributes
  - .github/workflows/ci.yml
  - .gitignore
  - Cargo.toml
  - README.md
excludes:
  - crates/__pycache__/
  - "*.pyc"
context: |
  This scope is the cross-crate workspace view.
  Use it for changes that span crate boundaries, workspace manifests, or top-level
  architecture decisions.

  Crate ownership:
  - `crates/sigil-abi`: the shared runtime ABI boundary
  - `crates/sigil-compiler`: the Sigil compiler pipeline and Wasm backend
  - `crates/sigil-runtime`: the Wasmtime actor host plus ephemeral tool runtime
  - `crates/sigil-registry`: the SQLite-backed template registry for ToolForge
  - `crates/sigil-cli`: the command line entry point over compiler, runtime, and registry

  Prefer the crate-local scopes for focused implementation work so agent context
  stays small and responsibilities remain clear.

  Current repository shape:
  - the compiler implements the Phase 2 language surface: generics and eager
    monomorphization, records/enums/arrays, actor messaging, two-ring checks,
    effect rows, taint tracking, typed FFI, region blocks, AIR lowering,
    capability and ownership verification, memory and fuel lowering, and Wasm
    emission
  - the runtime has two execution paths: `RuntimeHost` for actor-oriented Sigil
    modules and `execute_ephemeral` for one-shot outer-ring tool execution with
    I/O grants
  - the ABI crate owns shared import names and runtime metadata so compiler and
    runtime stay aligned without duplicating handoff structs
  - the registry crate stores reusable tool templates and metadata in SQLite for
    the CLI's `forge` and `registry` workflows
  - the CLI exposes compile/run commands plus ToolForge/template-registry flows
  - each major crate has a nested `src` scope so implementation work can stay local
  - repo-level hygiene is enforced with shared editor defaults, line-ending rules,
    and CI checks for `fmt`, `clippy`, and `test`
related:
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/.scope
  - crates/sigil-registry/.scope
  - crates/sigil-cli/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/src/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/src/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/src/.scope
  - crates/sigil-registry/src/.scope
  - crates/sigil-cli/src/.scope
tags:
  - workspace
  - crates
  - rust
  - toolforge
